@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1803 = private unnamed_addr constant [2294 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for methods that are annotated with a fixed return type which\0Ashould instead be returning `Self`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf methods that generally return `self` at runtime are annotated with a\0Afixed return type, and the class is subclassed, type checkers will not be\0Aable to infer the correct return type.\0A\0AFor example:\0A```python\0Aclass Shape:\0A    def set_scale(self, scale: float) -> Shape:\0A        self.scale = scale\0A        return self\0A\0Aclass Circle(Shape):\0A    def set_radius(self, radius: float) -> Circle:\0A        self.radius = radius\0A        return self\0A\0A# Type checker infers return type as `Shape`, not `Circle`.\0ACircle().set_scale(0.5)\0A\0A# Thus, this expression is invalid, as `Shape` has no attribute `set_radius`.\0ACircle().set_scale(0.5).set_radius(2.7)\0A```\0A\0ASpecifically, this check enforces that the return type of the following\0Amethods is `Self`:\0A\0A1. In-place binary-operation dunder methods, like `__iadd__`, `__imul__`, etc.\0A1. `__new__`, `__enter__`, and `__aenter__`, if those methods return the\0A   class name.\0A1. `__iter__` methods that return `Iterator`, despite the class inheriting\0A   directly from `Iterator`.\0A1. `__aiter__` methods that return `AsyncIterator`, despite the class\0A   inheriting directly from `AsyncIterator`.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __new__(cls, *args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Foo: ...\0A    def __enter__(self) -> Foo: ...\0A    async def __aenter__(self) -> Foo: ...\0A    def __iadd__(self, other: Foo) -> Foo: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing_extensions import Self\0A\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __new__(cls, *args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Self: ...\0A    def __enter__(self) -> Self: ...\0A    async def __aenter__(self) -> Self: ...\0A    def __iadd__(self, other: Foo) -> Self: ...\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe as it changes the meaning of your type annotations.\0A\0A## Availability\0A\0ABecause this rule relies on the third-party `typing_extensions` module for Python versions\0Abefore 3.11, its diagnostic will not be emitted, and no fix will be offered, if\0A`typing_extensions` imports have been disabled by the [`lint.typing-extensions`] linter option.\0A\0A## Options\0A\0A- `lint.typing-extensions`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.Self`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Self)\0A", align 1
