@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1810 = private unnamed_addr constant [411 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of type comments (e.g., `x = 1  # type: int`) in stub\0Afiles.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub (`.pyi`) files should use type annotations directly, rather\0Athan type comments, even if they're intended to support Python 2, since\0Astub files are not executed at runtime. The one exception is `# type: ignore`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Ax = 1  # type: int\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Ax: int = 1\0A```\0A", align 1
