@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1923 = private unnamed_addr constant [1230 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for extraneous blank lines.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APEP 8 recommends using blank lines as follows:\0A- No more than two blank lines between top-level statements.\0A- No more than one blank line between non-top-level statements.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef func1():\0A    pass\0A\0A\0A\0Adef func2():\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef func1():\0A    pass\0A\0A\0Adef func2():\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## Typing stub files (`.pyi`)\0AThe rule allows at most one blank line in typing stub files in accordance to the typing style guide recommendation.\0A\0ANote: The rule respects the following `isort` settings when determining the maximum number of blank lines allowed between two statements:\0A\0A* [`lint.isort.lines-after-imports`]: For top-level statements directly following an import statement.\0A* [`lint.isort.lines-between-types`]: For `import` statements directly following a `from ... import ...` statement or vice versa.\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.isort.lines-after-imports`\0A- `lint.isort.lines-between-types`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 8: Blank Lines](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#blank-lines)\0A- [Flake 8 rule](https://www.flake8rules.com/rules/E303.html)\0A- [Typing Style Guide](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/source/stubs.html#blank-lines)\0A", align 1
