@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2001 = private unnamed_addr constant [705 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of unused variables in function scopes.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA variable that is defined but not used is likely a mistake, and should\0Abe removed to avoid confusion.\0A\0AIf a variable is intentionally defined-but-not-used, it should be\0Aprefixed with an underscore, or some other value that adheres to the\0A[`lint.dummy-variable-rgx`] pattern.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    x = 1\0A    y = 2\0A    return x\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    x = 1\0A    return x\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe because removing an unused variable assignment may\0Adelete comments that are attached to the assignment.\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.dummy-variable-rgx`\0A", align 1
