@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2090 = private unnamed_addr constant [772 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for implicit class variables in dataclasses.\0A\0AVariables matching the [`lint.dummy-variable-rgx`] are excluded\0Afrom this rule.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AClass variables are shared between all instances of that class.\0AIn dataclasses, fields with no annotations at all\0Aare implicitly considered class variables, and a `TypeError` is\0Araised if a user attempts to initialize an instance of the class\0Awith this field.\0A\0A\0A```python\0A@dataclass\0Aclass C:\0A    a = 1\0A    b: str = \22\22\0A\0AC(a = 42)  # TypeError: C.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'a'\0A```\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0A@dataclass\0Aclass C:\0A    a = 1\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom typing import ClassVar\0A\0A\0A@dataclass\0Aclass C:\0A    a: ClassVar[int] = 1\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- [`lint.dummy-variable-rgx`]\0A", align 1
